## Why This Is Asked

Assesses the ability to architect privacy-aware computer vision systems under strict edge constraints while balancing accuracy and privacy guarantees. Requires concrete architecture, differentiable privacy terms, and rigorous evaluation plans.

## Key Concepts

- Privacy-preserving CV and de-identification modules
- Differentiable privacy loss and threat-model-aware evaluation
- Edge/on-device inference and latency budgeting
- Trade-offs between detection accuracy and privacy guarantees

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lightweight total loss combining detection accuracy and privacy
function computeTotalLoss(detectionPred, privacyPred, targets) {
    const detectionLoss = computeDetectionLoss(detectionPred, targets);
    const privacyLoss = computePrivacyLoss(privacyPred, targets.sensitiveRegions);

    // Weighted combination with privacy budget constraint
    return detectionLoss + lambdaPrivacy * privacyLoss;
}

// Differentiable de-identification module
class PrivacyModule {
    obfuscate(features, sensitiveRegions) {
        // Apply learnable obfuscation to sensitive regions
        return features.map((feat, i) => 
            sensitiveRegions[i] ? this.anonymize(feat) : feat
        );
    }
}
```

